#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184095 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184197 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8063bc9c-a10d-562b-93b1-508b4b26a674" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Singular Values of a Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "fcd3c46b-a87f-5ca8-9cf5-d9444a9c8218" :question/math-academy-id "e-8298" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. Any $1\\times4$ matrix $A$ has at most $1$ singular value.\n\nII. Any $4\\times2$ matrix $A$ has at most $2$ distinct singular values.\n\nIII. The matrix ![](images/b8/b8601b1e66ef1d302e7194f262f6a513063bba2114fb063c2fc16542d4684392.svg) has one negative singular value." :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix $A^T \\! A.$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since $A$ is a $1 \\times 4$ matrix and $A^T$ is a $4\\times 1$ matrix, $A^T \\! A$ must be a $4 \\times 4$ matrix: \n\n$$\n\\underset{\\bbox[Gainsboro, 2pt]{\\large 4} \\times {\\large 1}}{A^T} \\times \\underset{{\\large 1} \\times \\bbox[Gainsboro, 2pt]{\\large 4}}{A} =  \n\\underset{\\bbox[Gainsboro, 2pt]{\\large 4} \\times \\bbox[Gainsboro, 2pt]{\\large 4}}{A^T \\! A}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $4$ distinct singular values.\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $A$ is a $4 \\times 2$ matrix and $A^T$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix, $A^T \\! A$ must be a $2 \\times 2$ matrix: \n\n$$\n\\underset{\\bbox[Gainsboro, 2pt]{\\large 2} \\times {\\large 4}}{A^T} \\times \\underset{{\\large 4} \\times \\bbox[Gainsboro, 2pt]{\\large 2}}{A} = \n\\underset{\\bbox[Gainsboro, 2pt]{\\large 2} \\times \\bbox[Gainsboro, 2pt]{\\large 2}}{A^T \\! A}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $2$ distinct singular values.\n\n- Statement III is false. All singular values of any matrix are non-negative. So, $A$ cannot have a negative singular value.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184096 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184198 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2bf7196-b681-5ff6-bf16-24acefa04e6c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Singular Values of a Square Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "2b9ef509-4165-5772-81c1-9a3d78424dd1" :question/math-academy-id "e-8299" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix ![](images/85/85f9ccea6cd39f07174651d07316218edf50041f9d373e22cdaedf0c779caaf3.svg)" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix $A^T \\! A.$  \n\nFirst, we calculate $A^T \\! A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of $A^T \\! A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}5-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 4 & 5-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (5-\\lambda )^{2}-16 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-10\\lambda +9 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -1)(\\lambda -9) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =9,\\,1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{9}=3 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{1}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184097 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184199 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e70dec8f-9828-5fe7-bdb7-47e6557fc889" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Singular Values of a Rectangular Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "3fc137a7-9f7a-58de-ac92-1c7c2bdd53f9" :question/math-academy-id "e-8300" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix ![](images/59/590d5dc32950efa0fce63a5d64a5595210a3ccb08c613e364586dba4822d7314.svg)" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix $A^T \\! A.$  \n\nFirst, we calculate $A^T \\! A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of $A^T \\! A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}1-\\lambda  & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )\\begin{vmatrix}1-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix}+\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1-\\lambda  \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )^{2}-(1-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )((1-\\lambda )^{2}-1) & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ -\\lambda (\\lambda -1)(\\lambda -2) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =2,\\,1,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{2} \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{1}=1 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{3} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{3}}=\\sqrt{0}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367540 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184198 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2bf7196-b681-5ff6-bf16-24acefa04e6c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Singular Values of a Square Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11f72538-1df2-5400-9f78-cb8409f95ed7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367542} {:answer/id #uuid "aaed5f82-08d1-5931-9dc0-ef6782cb00fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ and $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367543} {:answer/id #uuid "85459f08-ebd2-5de2-af01-144d2aeb100c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ and $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367544} {:answer/id #uuid "d4be0251-97f5-5981-bda6-e62b677f0ba2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ and $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367545} {:answer/id #uuid "c7dc7fb6-4c25-5dc1-b337-7a9abd5eaf65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367546}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85459f08-ebd2-5de2-af01-144d2aeb100c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ and $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367544} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b11b93b-5ed4-5c27-8e1f-ae8a252505fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367541}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a7d5c241-f1dd-539c-bc82-e319298f04d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-139500" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}13 & 12 \\\\ 12 & 13\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}13-\\lambda  & 12 \\\\ 12 & 13-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (13-\\lambda )(13-\\lambda )-144 & =0 \\\\ 169-26\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-144 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-26\\lambda +25 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -1)(\\lambda -25) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =25,\\,1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{25}=5 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{1}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367547 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184199 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e70dec8f-9828-5fe7-bdb7-47e6557fc889" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Singular Values of a Rectangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "547cd0d6-fd5f-5b94-99cd-d4762af1fc66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5,0,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367549} {:answer/id #uuid "427695ad-2a8a-55af-9742-265b5d33144e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25,5,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367550} {:answer/id #uuid "49754909-9c5a-50e2-bda8-1f655927811b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5,5,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367551} {:answer/id #uuid "b92ac663-8b9a-5f7f-855b-b8691c3e6c16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5},0,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367552} {:answer/id #uuid "edca49b3-568f-5e5b-91e9-bd57fa31411b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5,1,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367553}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b92ac663-8b9a-5f7f-855b-b8691c3e6c16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5},0,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367552} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d25d269-9cbc-53c8-af16-a9f6f0118125" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367548}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "40fb180a-20af-5d07-ba44-09c0a1ca7e05" :question/math-academy-id "q-139512" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}1-\\lambda  & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ -\\lambda \\begin{vmatrix}4-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ -\\lambda [(1-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )-4)] & =0 \\\\ -\\lambda ({\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +4-4) & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}(\\lambda -5) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =5,\\,0,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{5} \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{0}=0 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{3} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{3}}=\\sqrt{0}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184876 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184198 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2bf7196-b681-5ff6-bf16-24acefa04e6c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Singular Values of a Square Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15ac2533-62db-535c-8dc9-3e42649cc9f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$10$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368873} {:answer/id #uuid "40993328-f48a-5d16-8477-6064543ac098" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$ and $0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368874} {:answer/id #uuid "02e843f4-0fc7-5f0b-a07b-3fa3bfc2abd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{10}$ and $0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368875} {:answer/id #uuid "98d65d3b-180c-559c-9c5f-db57ec8866a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368876} {:answer/id #uuid "f0117d76-d5c6-543b-9609-b905ac185a64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$10$ and $0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368877}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02e843f4-0fc7-5f0b-a07b-3fa3bfc2abd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{10}$ and $0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368875} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f0db150-06f0-53a7-8afc-b9734abea2f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368872}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5015d1af-a116-557e-a448-94566c652f07" :question/math-academy-id "q-94773" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}2-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 4 & 8-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(8-\\lambda )-16 & =0 \\\\ 16-2\\lambda -8\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-16 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-10\\lambda  & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -10) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =10,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{10} \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184877 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184198 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2bf7196-b681-5ff6-bf16-24acefa04e6c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Singular Values of a Square Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7d4ed93-75bb-5db0-9900-2362979d6c53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4,\\,3,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404734} {:answer/id #uuid "aac056f1-2c7a-51fc-b3b8-c7516856527b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3,\\,2,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404735} {:answer/id #uuid "2ef4562a-20e9-5af5-80a4-ced17b367b83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2,\\,2,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404736} {:answer/id #uuid "fd4157e7-a2cf-562a-af6a-fea80f5a7f86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16,\\,9,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404737} {:answer/id #uuid "95d80c78-37a1-5b82-8b12-a47780191024" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9,\\,4,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404738}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aac056f1-2c7a-51fc-b3b8-c7516856527b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3,\\,2,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404735} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce3dc232-fc1d-50e4-99b4-15ed1b8fa187" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404733}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e9152817-159b-5a54-868d-fe52d19640cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-94981" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -4 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}4-\\lambda  & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4-\\lambda  & -4 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 5-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )\\begin{vmatrix}4-\\lambda  & -4 \\\\ -4 & 5-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix}-2\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4-\\lambda  \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )((4-\\lambda )(5-\\lambda )-16)-4(4-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )(20-4\\lambda -5\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-16)-4(4-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-9\\lambda +4)-4(4-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-9\\lambda +4-4) & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-9\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -9) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =9,\\,4,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{9}=3 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{4}=2 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{3} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{3}}=\\sqrt{0}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184879 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184199 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e70dec8f-9828-5fe7-bdb7-47e6557fc889" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Singular Values of a Rectangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22d60bfe-9b93-5322-a886-7bb0f57eff46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5,\\,4,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508445} {:answer/id #uuid "2a9003af-2b01-57da-a933-16ff4579b8dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25,\\,4,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508455} {:answer/id #uuid "80e9ab77-14e2-509c-baf9-6e9048da53b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9,\\,4,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508580} {:answer/id #uuid "e99a56fa-1127-5a1f-872f-bba0b1b2c89b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3,\\,3,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508761} {:answer/id #uuid "ebe89adf-37a2-5724-a8e8-777891808839" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3,\\,2,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508767}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22d60bfe-9b93-5322-a886-7bb0f57eff46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5,\\,4,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508445} :answer-field/id #uuid "32eedbf9-e833-5743-ba35-1e838f8db9de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183883}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "421dde5b-98b5-58e5-8139-6656005b4621" :question/math-academy-id "q-94983" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & -12 \\\\ 0 & 16 & 0 \\\\ -12 & 0 & 16\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}9-\\lambda  & 0 & -12 \\\\ 0 & 16-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -12 & 0 & 16-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (16-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}9-\\lambda  & -12 \\\\ -12 & 16-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (16-\\lambda )((9-\\lambda )(16-\\lambda )-144) & =0 \\\\ (16-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-9\\lambda -16\\lambda +144-144) & =0 \\\\ (16-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-25\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -16)(\\lambda -25) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =25,\\,16,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{25}=5 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{16}=4 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{3} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{3}}=\\sqrt{0}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416485 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184197 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8063bc9c-a10d-562b-93b1-508b4b26a674" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Singular Values of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4129371-905f-54bf-ae87-c438b2fd43aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454184} {:answer/id #uuid "77bf2baa-cff5-52ce-8b41-e36aedb6e4a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454185}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77bf2baa-cff5-52ce-8b41-e36aedb6e4a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454185} :answer-field/id #uuid "861de6d8-648e-5127-85e8-5f06c2f6e1e5" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454842} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4731f9ee-31e7-5b9b-a569-ce496f29e4a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454186} {:answer/id #uuid "2b6665d1-709e-5474-aae8-a9d99f2ffbe8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454187}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b6665d1-709e-5474-aae8-a9d99f2ffbe8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454187} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5399265-62f4-5593-8a3d-8303b79fd15a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454843} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03d6caf3-6217-5f02-8760-2707cabb06a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454188} {:answer/id #uuid "7e82bf64-150d-5e41-acc3-db5ca4cb19c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454189}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03d6caf3-6217-5f02-8760-2707cabb06a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454188} :answer-field/id #uuid "416af97e-bb3e-58d1-b299-f595bb03d963" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454844}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e69dd032-aa5c-5891-a7fc-97b84703e88a" :question/math-academy-id "q-95261" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** Any $4\\times 3$ matrix $A$ has at most $3$ distinct singular values.\n- **II.** The singular values of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}$ are non-negative.\n- **III.** Any $3\\times 4$ matrix $A$ has at most $3$ distinct singular values." :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $A$ is a $4\\times 3$ matrix and ${A}^{T}$ is a $3\\times 4$ matrix, ${A}^{T}\\,A$ must be a $3\\times 3$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{{A}^{T}}_{3\\times 4}\\times {A}_{4\\times 3}={{A}^{T}\\,A}_{3\\times 3}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $3$ distinct singular values.\n\n- Statement II is true. All singular values of any matrix are non-negative.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is a $3\\times 4$ matrix and ${A}^{T}$ is a $4\\times 3$ matrix, ${A}^{T}\\,A$ must be a $4\\times 4$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{{A}^{T}}_{4\\times 3}\\times {A}_{3\\times 4}={{A}^{T}\\,A}_{4\\times 4}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $4$ distinct singular values.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543482 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184197 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8063bc9c-a10d-562b-93b1-508b4b26a674" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Singular Values of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "026e9975-ba0c-5eae-815a-fcd1e665b3d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542645} {:answer/id #uuid "79ac5216-69de-5dc4-a92b-b636df49e5d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542962} {:answer/id #uuid "7f21a217-b4f0-55ce-b377-f084a5b14d24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542982} {:answer/id #uuid "c2c913d4-93f7-5765-8bb6-090f7d52622b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543150} {:answer/id #uuid "e014b07e-27e4-516d-adc5-1ef689408d39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543210}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79ac5216-69de-5dc4-a92b-b636df49e5d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542962} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c3c93af-58f9-530c-baad-0a629ae81ede" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543298}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1e0723ce-a987-5c3e-a185-24b9f3aa7c5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-95270" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. Any $3\\times 4$ matrix $A$ has at most $4$ distinct singular values.\n\nII. Any $8\\times 6$ matrix $A$ has at most $8$ distinct singular values.\n\nIII. The matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]$ has one negative singular value." :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $A$ is a $3\\times 4$ matrix and ${A}^{T}$ is a $4\\times 3$ matrix, ${A}^{T}\\,A$ must be a $4\\times 4$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{{A}^{T}}_{4\\times 3}\\times {A}_{3\\times 4}={{A}^{T}\\,A}_{4\\times 4}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $4$ distinct singular values.\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $A$ is a $8\\times 6$ matrix and ${A}^{T}$ is a $6\\times 8$ matrix, ${A}^{T}\\,A$ must be a $6\\times 6$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{{A}^{T}}_{6\\times 8}\\times {A}_{8\\times 6}={{A}^{T}\\,A}_{6\\times 6}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $6$ distinct singular values.\n\n- Statement III is false.  All singular values of any matrix are non-negative. So, \n$A$  can't have a negative singular value.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416486 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184197 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8063bc9c-a10d-562b-93b1-508b4b26a674" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Singular Values of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17199cb6-adea-5b61-919d-b8c404e0acce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454196} {:answer/id #uuid "8d2c651a-9fde-5d68-8dc6-db31d39c222f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454197}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d2c651a-9fde-5d68-8dc6-db31d39c222f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454197} :answer-field/id #uuid "4075aa54-0dff-530d-8aaa-0316bbe68384" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454848} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ecfe78bb-58cf-5df3-9fec-25b0e56a5cf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454198} {:answer/id #uuid "1cdaafa5-1a83-54e7-855b-cedee6333689" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454199}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ecfe78bb-58cf-5df3-9fec-25b0e56a5cf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454198} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebe209e3-0b27-5e04-917c-a2a111895c0f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454849} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72750c08-7405-534f-a4d7-2b63080f7417" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454200} {:answer/id #uuid "cf58434d-bb62-5004-8244-73fdeaf3e6f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454201}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72750c08-7405-534f-a4d7-2b63080f7417" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454200} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b11c932-8a01-5b51-9317-14a5c84895c3" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454850}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fef86daf-091a-52fa-bcf0-1d2b609bb348" :question/math-academy-id "q-95281" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** Any $6\\times 3$ matrix $A$ has at most $3$ distinct singular values.\n- **II.** The matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$ has one negative singular value.\n- **III.** Any $4\\times 5$ matrix $A$ has at most $4$ distinct singular values." :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, since $A$ is a $6\\times 3$ matrix and ${A}^{T}$ is a $3\\times 6$ matrix, ${A}^{T}\\,A$ must be a $3\\times 3$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{{A}^{T}}_{3\\times 6}\\times {A}_{6\\times 3}={{A}^{T}\\,A}_{3\\times 3}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $3$ distinct singular values.\n\n- Statement II is false. All singular values of any matrix are non-negative. So, $A$ can't have a negative singular value.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is a $4\\times 5$ matrix and ${A}^{T}$ is a $5\\times 4$ matrix, ${A}^{T}\\,A$ must be a $5\\times 5$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{{A}^{T}}_{5\\times 4}\\times {A}_{4\\times 5}={{A}^{T}\\,A}_{5\\times 5}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $5$ distinct singular values.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543511 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184197 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8063bc9c-a10d-562b-93b1-508b4b26a674" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Singular Values of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09638aaf-77e9-5651-870e-522b6cc8115f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542658} {:answer/id #uuid "1d848745-0d69-5731-947e-0a9ae11809b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542715} {:answer/id #uuid "aa4333dc-3ea2-5e37-ab50-ec3e34c12a9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543088} {:answer/id #uuid "c588edce-5cf5-501a-93b4-d2734b483461" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543157} {:answer/id #uuid "db2d98c7-af14-5f48-be6c-f11b82999c7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543200}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa4333dc-3ea2-5e37-ab50-ec3e34c12a9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543088} :answer-field/id #uuid "a29f2b28-9204-5899-8070-b3f5ffe02498" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543407}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "66207faf-3d6b-5406-8c58-c05d9d84a48f" :question/math-academy-id "q-95283" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ has one negative singular value.\n\nII. Any $2\\times 4$ matrix $A$ has at most $4$ distinct singular values.\n\nIII. Any $6\\times 3$ matrix $A$ has at most $6$ distinct singular values." :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false.  All singular values of any matrix are non-negative. So, \n$A$  can't have any negative singular value.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,  since $A$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix and ${A}^{T}$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix, ${A}^{T}\\,A$ must be a $4\\times 4$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{{A}^{T}}_{4\\times 2}\\times {A}_{2\\times 4}={{A}^{T}\\,A}_{4\\times 4}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $4$ distinct singular values.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is a $6\\times 3$ matrix and ${A}^{T}$ is a $3\\times 6$ matrix, ${A}^{T}\\,A$ must be a $3\\times 3$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{{A}^{T}}_{3\\times 6}\\times {A}_{6\\times 3}={{A}^{T}\\,A}_{3\\times 3}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $3$ distinct singular values.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368899 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184197 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8063bc9c-a10d-562b-93b1-508b4b26a674" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Singular Values of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2dd7d102-aedc-5e91-a047-f8cad7922fa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452179} {:answer/id #uuid "92081811-29e7-5671-8299-e57c420e3eed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452180}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2dd7d102-aedc-5e91-a047-f8cad7922fa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452179} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8ec87bb-4b3c-5297-b2b5-774e119551e7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452937} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f401cf9-efdd-54a5-8b7a-61de53c5e100" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452181} {:answer/id #uuid "d311e63e-ec0f-59e7-bd16-ff6db836531a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452182}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f401cf9-efdd-54a5-8b7a-61de53c5e100" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452181} :answer-field/id #uuid "968b4eb6-8e02-5cf8-a607-4efe45260c79" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452938} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "097bc3b9-dca8-57a1-8757-cc94a3779994" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452183} {:answer/id #uuid "862c2197-4e1a-56eb-9ab6-61a342ae1dbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452184}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "862c2197-4e1a-56eb-9ab6-61a342ae1dbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452184} :answer-field/id #uuid "60e094a4-a998-50ed-b26d-1c216b5e4e7c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452939}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4e856448-81c6-5a27-b63c-c2864d6eca93" :question/math-academy-id "q-95291" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** Any matrix of the form  $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-a & 0 \\\\ 0 & a\\end{bmatrix}$ has one negative singular value.\n- **II.** Any $5\\times 2$ matrix $A$ has at most $5$ distinct singular values.\n- **III.** Any $4\\times 5$ matrix $A$ has at most $5$ distinct singular values." :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false.  All singular values of any matrix are non-negative. So, \n$A$  can't have any negative singular value.\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $A$ is a $5\\times 2$ matrix and ${A}^{T}$ is a $2\\times 5$ matrix, ${A}^{T}\\,A$ must be a $2\\times 2$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{{A}^{T}}_{2\\times 5}\\times {A}_{5\\times 2}={{A}^{T}\\,A}_{2\\times 2}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $2$ distinct singular values.\n\n- Statement III is true.  Indeed,  since $A$ is a $4\\times 5$ matrix and ${A}^{T}$ is a $5\\times 4$ matrix, ${A}^{T}\\,A$ must be a $5\\times 5$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{{A}^{T}}_{5\\times 4}\\times {A}_{4\\times 5}={{A}^{T}\\,A}_{5\\times 5}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $5$ distinct singular values.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368906 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184199 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e70dec8f-9828-5fe7-bdb7-47e6557fc889" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Singular Values of a Rectangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5aacda77-04a2-5890-a544-02a590c4abbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{10}$ and $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368908} {:answer/id #uuid "d7d351a9-304d-59f9-bb2a-64ac42ed426b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ and $0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368909} {:answer/id #uuid "37198688-7720-5bf5-9d97-18a4fc4f1eae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$25$ and $0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368910} {:answer/id #uuid "11993b50-f9b2-5859-af25-cf8175b4ff5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{5}$ and $0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368911} {:answer/id #uuid "4633659c-497d-54ae-9280-c13bf99f6b0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$25$ and $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368912}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7d351a9-304d-59f9-bb2a-64ac42ed426b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ and $0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368909} :answer-field/id #uuid "08930f82-1a1a-57e2-874c-8663b93ed935" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368907}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bc0c7469-fdf7-5096-ab3b-9c5617b672e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-95316" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 12 \\\\ 12 & 16\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}9-\\lambda  & 12 \\\\ 12 & 16-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (9-\\lambda )(16-\\lambda )-144 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-9\\lambda -16\\lambda +144-144 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-25\\lambda  & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -25) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =25,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{25}=5 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415576 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184198 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2bf7196-b681-5ff6-bf16-24acefa04e6c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Singular Values of a Square Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "226f1dbb-e586-5c42-93b7-43b8c5544971" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4,\\,3,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415547} {:answer/id #uuid "4f6c601f-dc07-56ea-bef7-25b4a444358f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15,\\,9,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415550} {:answer/id #uuid "6266bf60-cbee-534e-aaad-f1b70c7c6e56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5,\\,4,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415552} {:answer/id #uuid "e2b2ea65-38c0-59e1-8092-216f0cd8d2d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9,\\,4,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415566} {:answer/id #uuid "f993a82a-65cc-57a6-9da0-7876fb553640" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3,\\,2,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415568}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f993a82a-65cc-57a6-9da0-7876fb553640" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3,\\,2,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415568} :answer-field/id #uuid "9da244a1-6637-5db7-b8ef-33283dce2b41" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415572}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "42bc3fa3-d1ed-5eee-8e63-dbe17bc3a3c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-95349" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}8-\\lambda  & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (-\\lambda )\\begin{vmatrix}8-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (-\\lambda )((8-\\lambda )(5-\\lambda )-4) & =0 \\\\ (-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda +36) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -9) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =9,\\,4,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{9}=3 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{4}=2 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{3} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{3}}=\\sqrt{0}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186404787 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184199 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e70dec8f-9828-5fe7-bdb7-47e6557fc889" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Singular Values of a Rectangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "684d0d7c-6c21-5d44-b7c3-71eab50414a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5,\\,3,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404789} {:answer/id #uuid "1cb76c1a-945d-5de9-8a45-072766c1ef8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3},\\,1,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404790} {:answer/id #uuid "b7a6892e-2b71-58c4-8195-ae2ebdcda46b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5},\\,2,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404791} {:answer/id #uuid "caa0c8c7-3e7b-52f8-87b0-6d3a1f9c7cb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3,\\,1,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404792} {:answer/id #uuid "c5d3a286-9f2e-5033-b1c0-5b409e80ea4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5,\\,2,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404793}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1cb76c1a-945d-5de9-8a45-072766c1ef8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3},\\,1,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404790} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a494b6c-01e8-55d5-b122-0aa7d1180b90" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404788}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ae342c4d-42b7-5fdb-833c-f679170c12f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-95354" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}2-\\lambda  & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1-\\lambda  & 0\\end{vmatrix}+(1-\\lambda )\\begin{vmatrix}2-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ -(1-\\lambda )+(1-\\lambda )[(2-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-1)] & =0 \\\\ -(1-\\lambda )+(1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-3\\lambda +1) & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-3\\lambda +1-1) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (1-\\lambda )(\\lambda -3) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =3,\\,1,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{3} \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{1}=1 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{3} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{3}}=\\sqrt{0}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416484 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184199 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e70dec8f-9828-5fe7-bdb7-47e6557fc889" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Singular Values of a Rectangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4889279a-9659-5dae-8259-b1442e0b8893" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416445} {:answer/id #uuid "a08ff49c-3e48-5969-9cc0-4603170a0646" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{3}$ and $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416462} {:answer/id #uuid "b8b05a8d-1f8d-58ee-8ab2-e2cf7750d0f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$9$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416464} {:answer/id #uuid "c7d2dbc4-67b2-5124-9e27-6ec2f6fd08b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{3}$ and $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416466} {:answer/id #uuid "e93e9e61-f7d3-5cb6-85a3-a9059ed558a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$9$ and $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416470}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4889279a-9659-5dae-8259-b1442e0b8893" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416445} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd7054d7-ed2b-5613-b2fc-90c17c4791c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416478}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c791e385-b793-500d-9a77-3e468ca25a09" :question/math-academy-id "q-95359" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}5-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ -2 & 8-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (5-\\lambda )(8-\\lambda )-4 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-8\\lambda -5\\lambda +40-4 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda +36 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -9) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =9,\\,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{9}=3 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{4}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415575 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184198 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2bf7196-b681-5ff6-bf16-24acefa04e6c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Singular Values of a Square Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03cdbbac-81f1-5a5a-8c0b-cc9eada2874c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8$ and $5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415544} {:answer/id #uuid "62cb00c2-7471-5b2f-86f0-ee1821df8b74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{3}$ and $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415553} {:answer/id #uuid "903124f2-18ad-506a-90f1-7a04c1d43894" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$ and $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415559} {:answer/id #uuid "a9a954e9-faca-5755-872b-2adf607495f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{5}$ and $\\sqrt{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415561} {:answer/id #uuid "e9b697fb-7c5f-5191-9456-d6dcf71e2749" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{8}$ and $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415567}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9b697fb-7c5f-5191-9456-d6dcf71e2749" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{8}$ and $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415567} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ee60de8-7912-55ad-80bc-fd51fae2e264" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415570}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "35756e17-7ddb-5db3-9246-f082e3b776e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-95362" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}8-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (8-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =8,\\,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{8} \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
